    # For two functions i and j, placing i outside j is at least as good
    # exactly when (A_i - 1) / B_i >= (A_j - 1) / B_j.
    # Thus an optimal sequence is in nondecreasing ratio order when
    # processed from the innermost function to the outermost one.
